0:{"buildId":"JFSdapXluxcZ7WLb1GQKv","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"caseData":{"level":"RED","case_id":"R003","title":"Twenty and Already Winning?","short_summary":"A polished post about money, discipline, and success pulls young viewers into a heated comparison over who is falling behind.","duration_min":15,"skills":["Visual evidence","Language and claims","Information chains"],"spotted_url":"/assets/images/R003/R003_spotted.png","theme":["Social media","Personal finance"],"story_context":"A post by a young 'Minh Khang' persona pairs financial advice with an aspirational lifestyle photo. Its message is drawing admiration, defensiveness, and comparison among viewers. Examine the post before deciding how much weight it deserves.","modules":{"step_1_image_forensics":{"mechanic_type":"IMAGE_FORENSICS","image_url":"/assets/images/R003/R003_fake.jpg","image_width":1402,"image_height":1122,"context_text":"This photo supports Minh Khang's claims about his luxury lifestyle. Examine whether its physical details remain internally consistent.","target_anomalies":[{"anomaly_id":"R003_IMG_01","name":"inconsistent_hand_features","x_pct":38.7,"y_pct":58.2,"radius_pct":8.6,"socratic_quiz":{"question":"Which comparison would be most useful when examining the phone-holding hand?","options":["A. Check whether perspective alone explains why the hand appears larger than the wrist.","B. Check whether its color and knuckle contours transition naturally from the wrist through the grip.","C. Check whether the phone angle points in the same direction as the person's gaze."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"Perspective can explain size, but not inconsistent color or joint structure. Compare the hand-to-wrist transition and treat the mismatch as a clue, not proof."},"description":"The phone-holding hand has a subtly over-saturated, waxy color and knuckle contours that do not fully align with a natural grip."},{"anomaly_id":"R003_IMG_02","name":"warped_window_frame","x_pct":17,"y_pct":49.9,"radius_pct":11.2,"socratic_quiz":{"question":"Which check would best distinguish perspective from an inconsistency in the window area?","options":["A. Compare the frame's brightness with the buildings visible outside.","B. Trace whether the rigid frame and handle keep smooth contours or ripple independently along their length.","C. Check whether the handle is positioned at a practical height for opening the window."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"Perspective may tilt a rigid object, but its edges should remain structurally coherent. Compare the waviness with the rest of the frame and a genuine window."},"description":"The rigid window frame and handle develop uneven, wavy contours instead of preserving consistent manufactured geometry."}]},"step_2_text_highlight":{"mechanic_type":"TEXT_HIGHLIGHT","simulated_post":{"author":"Minh Khang","time_posted":"2 hours ago","content":"It's honestly funny how some people keep saying \"money doesn't buy happiness\" every time someone posts something nice. Like... just because you can't afford it doesn't mean it's \"showing off.\" Meanwhile, everyone I know is out here grinding, getting internships, buying what they want, and actually doing something with their lives. If you're still making excuses while everyone else is moving up, maybe stop blaming other people and ask yourself why you're getting left behind. Stay mad if you want, but don't expect the world to wait for you."},"traps":[{"trap_id":"R003_T1","ground_truth_start":127,"ground_truth_end":192,"matched_text":"just because you can't afford it doesn't mean it's \"showing off.\"","weapon_type":["attacking_motive","strawman"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"Which response evaluates the criticism without guessing the speaker's motive?","options":["A. Check whether the critic has previously posted about money.","B. Check whether the criticism names specific behavior and applies a reasonable standard.","C. Check whether most commenters describe the critic as jealous or sincere."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"A guessed motive does not determine whether criticism is valid. Evaluate its claim and evidence first."}},{"trap_id":"R003_T2","ground_truth_start":204,"ground_truth_end":331,"matched_text":"everyone I know is out here grinding, getting internships, buying what they want, and actually doing something with their lives","weapon_type":["false_comparison"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"What data would be needed to test the claim that buying luxury goods means greater success?","options":["A. The average price of the products shown in the post.","B. A clear measure of success plus data on income, debt, family support, and starting conditions.","C. The number of the writer's acquaintances who liked or shared the post."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"Buying power does not automatically measure success. A meaningful comparison needs a shared measure and comparable starting conditions."}},{"trap_id":"R003_T3","ground_truth_start":333,"ground_truth_end":477,"matched_text":"If you're still making excuses while everyone else is moving up, maybe stop blaming other people and ask yourself why you're getting left behind","weapon_type":["inducing_fomo","personal_attack"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"What evidence is needed before believing that 'everyone is moving up while you fall behind'?","options":["A. A feed containing many popular posts about shopping and travel.","B. Representative data about the group, including unposted outcomes and relevant circumstances.","C. The reader's anxiety after seeing several similar posts in a row."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"A feed shows what people choose to publish, not a representative sample. Do not turn the feeling of falling behind into a factual conclusion."}},{"trap_id":"R003_T4","ground_truth_start":479,"ground_truth_end":543,"matched_text":"Stay mad if you want, but don't expect the world to wait for you","weapon_type":["emotional_dismissal"],"socratic_quiz":{"question":"What does 'stay mad' do to a criticism that includes evidence?","options":["A. It asks the critic to provide clearer evidence before the discussion continues.","B. It recasts the criticism as an emotional reaction so its substance can be ignored.","C. It acknowledges the critic's feelings and invites further explanation."],"correct_option":"B","explanation":"Labeling an emotion does not answer an objection. Return to the argument and evidence instead of diagnosing the speaker."}}]},"step_3_sorting_game":{"mechanic_type":"DRAG_AND_DROP_SORTING","context_text":"A post by a young 'Minh Khang' persona pairs financial advice with an aspirational lifestyle photo. Its message is drawing admiration, defensiveness, and comparison among viewers. Examine the post before deciding how much weight it deserves.","pool_items":[{"item_id":"R003_SORT_01","text":"Readers experience intense FOMO and self-doubt, fearing they are falling behind their peers."},{"item_id":"R003_SORT_02","text":"The influencer posts fabricated AI images of luxury items to establish fake status and authority."},{"item_id":"R003_SORT_03","text":"The influencer pitches an expensive 'wealth mindset masterclass' as the ultimate shortcut to success."},{"item_id":"R003_SORT_04","text":"The post uses false comparisons and condescending language to demean normal working youth as 'lazy'."}],"correct_sequence":["R003_SORT_02","R003_SORT_04","R003_SORT_01","R003_SORT_03"],"validation_feedback":{"success":"Correct! You have decoded the classic toxic flexing funnel: Fabricate status (Hook) → Belittle through false comparisons (Attack) → Trigger insecurity and FOMO (Anxiety) → Sell an expensive 'shortcut' course (Monetization).","failure":"Incorrect sequence. Toxic flexing manipulators first establish fake wealth, then attack the audience's self-esteem to create FOMO before offering their paid course as a fake solution."}}},"dialogue_trigger":{"question":"Ask your Teacher/Parent: If a social media post makes you feel anxious that you are falling behind your peers who seem to afford luxury lifestyles, what steps can you take to evaluate what is real versus staged?","mil_insight":"Social media highlights rarely reflect full reality, and AI image tools make lavish lifestyles effortless to fake. Remind youth that success is not measured by material flexing or belittling others, and urgent pitches for expensive 'mindset courses' are almost always predatory scams."}}}],["$L3","$L4","$L5"],"$L6"]}],"isPartial":"$@7","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L9","isPartial":"$@a","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$Lb","isPartial":"$@c","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":"$d"},{"rsc":"$Le","isPartial":"$@f","staleTime":"$8","varyParams":"$d"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@10","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@11"}
